  "review_notes": [
    "The two *and*s inside *to and fro* and *up and down* are internal to single morphemes' fixed renderings and are not clause connectives; rule 14's closing sentence decides this by asking what stands on either side of the English word in the Hebrew.",
    "אֵי מִזֶּה is split rather than fused because the ASV writes a word for each of אֵי and מִן; only the demonstrative goes unrepresented."
